{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>He.</b> Does these things." "<b>Shall dwell.</b> In Zion, as though he dwells in fortresses." "<b>His bread is given.</b> Bread will be given him to sustain him." "<b>Trusted.</b> That will not fail, and the meaning is that they will not be cut off; and so he dwells in rest, and also delights."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:56:30.629811767Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}